---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: ""
description: "Project Broadsheet is a free, open-source way to run your own publication online — a home page, sections, an archive, and reading tools that readers notice. Yours to keep."
permalink: /index.html
---
<section class="hero">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="hero__inner">
      <div>
        <span class="hero__eyebrow">Free · Open-source</span>
        <h1 class="hero__title">{{ meta.tagline }}</h1>
        <p class="hero__subhead">{{ meta.subhead }}</p>
        <div class="hero__actions btn-group btn-group--balanced">
          <a class="btn btn--primary btn--lg" href="{{ meta.liveExample }}" rel="noopener">See a real example →</a>
          <a class="btn btn--outline btn--lg" href="#what-you-get">How it works</a>
        </div>
        <div class="social-strip social-strip--hero">
          <div class="social-strip__inner">
            <span class="social-strip__item">Live at <strong><a href="{{ meta.liveExample }}">{{ meta.liveExampleName }}</a></strong></span>
            <span class="social-strip__item">Code on <strong><a href="{{ meta.github }}">GitHub</a></strong></span>
            <span class="social-strip__item">Free to use, forever</span>
            <span class="social-strip__item">Your writing stays yours</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <hr class="gold-rule hero__rule">
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="home-features" id="what-you-get">
  <div class="container">
    <header class="home-features__header">
      <span class="eyebrow">What it is</span>
      <h2 class="home-features__title">A website for your writing, without the middlemen.</h2>
      <p class="home-features__summary">If you've ever wanted a proper home for your writing — one that looks like a publication rather than a blog, doesn't charge a monthly fee, and can't be taken away by the company that hosts it — this is for you. You bring the words. Project Broadsheet handles everything else a publication needs.</p>
    </header>

    <div class="home-features__grid">
      <article class="feature-card">
        <h3 class="feature-card__title">A home page and sections</h3>
        <p class="feature-card__summary">A polished front page, plus separate pages for the kinds of writing you do — news, opinion, reviews, essays, whatever fits. Each one gets its own index and feed that readers can follow.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="feature-card">
        <h3 class="feature-card__title">A searchable archive</h3>
        <p class="feature-card__summary">Everything you publish is kept, dated, and searchable. Readers can find an older piece in seconds. No posts disappear behind a paywall or get lost in a feed.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="feature-card">
        <h3 class="feature-card__title">A newsletter, if you want one</h3>
        <p class="feature-card__summary">A sign-up form in the footer, connected to a small independent email service (Buttondown). Your subscriber list belongs to you — take it with you any time.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="feature-card">
        <h3 class="feature-card__title">Thoughtful touches for readers</h3>
        <p class="feature-card__summary">Dark mode. Save-for-later bookmarks. Highlights and notes that stay on the reader's own device. The small things serious publications have, and personal sites rarely do.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="feature-card">
        <h3 class="feature-card__title">An author page for every writer</h3>
        <p class="feature-card__summary">Each contributor gets a page with a short bio and everything they've written. Readers can follow a specific writer, not just the whole publication.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="feature-card">
        <h3 class="feature-card__title">Made to last</h3>
        <p class="feature-card__summary">No database, no login system, nothing that falls over when a server hiccups. The whole site is plain files — fast, cheap to host, and easy to move somewhere else if you ever want to.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section-alt">
  <div class="container">
    <header class="home-features__header">
      <span class="eyebrow">Who it's for</span>
      <h2 class="home-features__title">Independent writers and small teams.</h2>
    </header>

    <div class="home-features__grid">
      <article class="feature-card">
        <h3 class="feature-card__title">A writer starting out</h3>
        <p class="feature-card__summary">You want a real website for your work, not another account on someone else's platform.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="feature-card">
        <h3 class="feature-card__title">A small magazine or newsroom</h3>
        <p class="feature-card__summary">A handful of people publishing together, who'd rather put their budget into reporting than into software.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="feature-card">
        <h3 class="feature-card__title">A student paper or classroom</h3>
        <p class="feature-card__summary">Teachers and students running a publication as part of learning. Everything is free and no one needs an account.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="feature-card">
        <h3 class="feature-card__title">Someone leaving a newsletter platform</h3>
        <p class="feature-card__summary">You've outgrown Substack or Medium and want your archive, your readers, and your work on a site you own.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="container">
    <header class="home-features__header">
      <span class="eyebrow">How you use it</span>
      <h2 class="home-features__title">Write, save, publish.</h2>
      <p class="home-features__summary">You don't need to be a developer. If you can format an email, you can run a publication on Project Broadsheet. There's no dashboard to log into and no software to install on a server.</p>
    </header>
    <div class="how-it-works">
      <div class="step">
        <div class="step__num">1</div>
        <div>
          <div class="step__title">Write</div>
          <p class="step__body">Each article is a plain text file, written in a simple formatting style called Markdown — essentially typing an email with a few light conventions for headings, links, and images.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="step">
        <div class="step__num">2</div>
        <div>
          <div class="step__title">Save</div>
          <p class="step__body">Your writing lives in a folder on your computer, and a copy is kept online so nothing is ever lost. Every change is recorded, so you can always look back at an earlier version.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="step">
        <div class="step__num">3</div>
        <div>
          <div class="step__title">Publish</div>
          <p class="step__body">When you're ready, the site rebuilds itself in under a minute on a free host. Your readers see the update, the search index refreshes, and the newsletter (if you use one) can go out on the same schedule.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div style="text-align: center; margin-top: var(--space-xl);">
      <a class="btn btn--outline" href="/docs/getting-started/">Read the getting-started guide</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section-alt">
  <div class="container">
    <header class="home-features__header">
      <span class="eyebrow">What it costs</span>
      <h2 class="home-features__title">Close to nothing.</h2>
      <p class="home-features__summary">The whole yearly bill for a publication running on Project Broadsheet is usually the price of a domain name. No platform fees, no per-subscriber charges, no revenue share.</p>
    </header>
    <div class="home-features__grid">
      <article class="feature-card">
        <h3 class="feature-card__title">Project Broadsheet itself</h3>
        <p class="feature-card__summary">Free. Always. Use it for anything, including paid publications, with no restrictions.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="feature-card">
        <h3 class="feature-card__title">A place online for the site</h3>
        <p class="feature-card__summary">Free on services like Cloudflare Pages or Netlify, up to very generous limits that most independent publications never hit.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="feature-card">
        <h3 class="feature-card__title">A domain name</h3>
        <p class="feature-card__summary">Around $10–15 a year from any registrar. This is the one part you pay for, because it's yours.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="feature-card">
        <h3 class="feature-card__title">A newsletter service</h3>
        <p class="feature-card__summary">Free up to a hundred subscribers on Buttondown, then modest flat fees after that. Only needed if you actually run a newsletter.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{% if showcase and showcase.length %}
<section class="section">
  <div class="container">
    <header class="home-features__header">
      <span class="eyebrow">In the wild</span>
      <h2 class="home-features__title">Sites already running on it</h2>
      <p class="home-features__summary">Seeing a real publication is worth more than a list of features. Have a look around.</p>
    </header>
    <div class="grid grid-2" style="max-width: 44rem; margin-inline: auto;">
      {% for s in showcase %}
      <a class="showcase-card" href="{{ s.url }}">
        <div class="showcase-card__image">{{ s.name }}</div>
        <div class="showcase-card__body">
          <div class="card__title">{{ s.name }}</div>
          <p class="card__summary">{{ s.summary }}</p>
        </div>
      </a>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
{% endif %}

<section class="section section-sunken">
  <div class="container" style="max-width: 44rem; text-align: center;">
    <h2 class="home-features__title">A project, not a product.</h2>
    <p class="home-features__summary">Project Broadsheet is made and maintained in the open by one person. You can read every line of code, take it in your own direction, or simply use it as-is. If you build a publication with it, I'd love to see it.</p>
    <div class="btn-group btn-group--balanced btn-group--center" style="margin-top: var(--space-lg);">
      <a class="btn btn--outline" href="/about/">About the project</a>
      <a class="btn btn--outline" href="{{ meta.github }}" rel="noopener">View the source</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
